---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../styles/portfolio-v3.css";
import "../styles/integrity.css";
import career from "../../data/research-operations-positioning.mjs";

const { D } = career;
const pageTitle = "Sensitive Qualitative Research Operations — Mario Marcolongo";
const pageDescription = "Evidence-bound case study of volunteer focus-group facilitation and research-operations support in a University of Padua project involving autistic participants and sensitive sexuality and relationship topics.";
const thesisUrl = "https://thesis.unipd.it/handle/20.500.12608/51396";
const supervisorUrl = "https://dpss.unipd.it/en/node/239";
const departmentUrl = "https://www.unipd.it/en/dpss";
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} canonical="https://mariomarcolongo.com/research-operations.html">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,follow" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "ProfilePage",
      name: pageTitle,
      description: pageDescription,
      url: "https://mariomarcolongo.com/research-operations.html",
      mainEntity: { "@id": "https://mariomarcolongo.com/#person" },
      about: ["Qualitative research operations", "Focus-group facilitation", "Accessible research", "Participant privacy", "Autism research"]
    })}></script>
  </Fragment>

  <SiteNav activePage="integrity" />

  <main class="v3-page integrity-page">
    <section class="integrity-hero">
      <div class="v3-kicker">Research operations · evidence boundary</div>
      <h1>Sensitive qualitative research requires accessibility, privacy and exact attribution.</h1>
      <p>I report a volunteer role supporting remote focus groups with autistic participants discussing sexuality and relationships. The public University of Padua thesis documents the project and parts of its methodology, but it does not identify the individual facilitators. This page separates those two evidence levels.</p>
      <div class="v3-hero-actions">
        <a class="v3-button v3-button-primary" href="/cv-editorial.html">Research & Editorial CV →</a>
        <a class="v3-button" href="/cv-integrity.html">Knowledge Integrity CV</a>
        <a class="v3-button v3-button-quiet" href="/integrity.html">Other evidence records</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="integrity-principles" aria-label="Evidence status">
      <article><strong>Project corroborated</strong><span>An institutional thesis documents the study, ethics approval and focus-group procedure.</span></article>
      <article><strong>Role self-reported</strong><span>The thesis does not name Mario Marcolongo or the individual facilitators.</span></article>
      <article><strong>Privacy preserved</strong><span>No participant identities, private correspondence or confidential session content are published.</span></article>
      <article><strong>Scope limited</strong><span>This is research-operations experience, not authorship of the thesis or ownership of its findings.</span></article>
    </section>

    <section class="v3-section" id="reported-contribution">
      <div class="v3-section-head">
        <div>
          <div class="v3-kicker">Reported contribution</div>
          <h2>Volunteer facilitation and operational support.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The role is described conservatively as a contribution to study operations rather than as academic authorship or independent research leadership.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="integrity-record sensitive-research-operations">
        <div class="integrity-record-number">01</div>
        <div class="integrity-record-main">
          <div class="integrity-record-category">Sensitive qualitative research operations</div>
          <h3>Autism and sexuality focus groups</h3>
          <p class="integrity-context">Volunteer collaboration under Marta Panzeri at the University of Padua Department of Developmental Psychology and Socialisation, reported for November 2022–2025.</p>
          <div class="integrity-record-columns">
            <div>
              <h4>Work reported</h4>
              <ul>
                <li>Served as lead or co-facilitator across approximately 4–5 recorded Zoom sessions, typically lasting 1–2 hours, with autistic participants discussing sensitive sexuality and relationship topics.</li>
                <li>Helped develop and operationalize procedures covering consent, pseudonymous naming, optional captions and written-chat participation, structured prompts, timed turns, recording boundaries and two-person facilitation handoffs.</li>
                <li>Supported participant recruitment, bibliographic research, technical preparation and protocol feedback from an autistic perspective.</li>
                <li>Worked with the supervisor, researchers and another autistic volunteer facilitator while keeping participant information and session content confidential.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Capabilities demonstrated</h4>
              <div class="v3-methods">
                <span>Qualitative research operations</span>
                <span>Sensitive-topic facilitation</span>
                <span>Accessibility-aware participation</span>
                <span>Consent and privacy procedures</span>
                <span>Participant recruitment</span>
                <span>Two-person moderation</span>
              </div>
              <div class="integrity-limit">
                <strong>Evidence boundary</strong>
                <p>These responsibilities are self-reported. The linked thesis corroborates the institutional project and several methodological features, but it does not attribute the role to Mario Marcolongo, verify every listed responsibility or independently confirm the approximate number of sessions he facilitated.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="v3-section" id="public-context">
      <div class="v3-section-head">
        <div>
          <div class="v3-kicker">Public corroboration</div>
          <h2>What the institutional record supports.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The public record is useful because it confirms the project context and methodology without being misrepresented as individual attribution.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="integrity-method-grid">
        <article class="integrity-method">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Institutional output</h3>
          <p>The University of Padua archive publishes Gabriele Conti’s 2022/2023 bachelor’s thesis, supervised by Marta Panzeri, on sensory differences and sexuality among autistic people.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="integrity-method">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Study procedure</h3>
          <p>The thesis describes remote Zoom focus groups with conductors and co-conductors, including two autistic facilitators intended to support participant comfort.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="integrity-method">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Accessibility and privacy</h3>
          <p>The public methodology includes optional camera use, microphone or written-chat participation, an approved ethics protocol and deletion of recordings after transcription.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="integrity-method">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Attribution limit</h3>
          <p>The thesis names its author and supervisor but does not publish the identities of the individual facilitators. It therefore cannot serve as direct proof of Mario’s participation.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="v3-hero-actions">
        <a class="v3-button v3-button-primary" href={thesisUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect public thesis context ↗</a>
        <a class="v3-button" href={supervisorUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Marta Panzeri profile ↗</a>
        <a class="v3-button v3-button-quiet" href={departmentUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">University department ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="integrity-ethics">
      <div>
        <div class="v3-kicker">Career relevance</div>
        <h2>Strongest for research and community operations.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>This case supports applications involving qualitative research operations, participant research, community engagement, accessibility-aware facilitation, human-data programs and sensitive-topic moderation.</p>
        <p>It is supporting—not flagship—evidence for knowledge-integrity work, and it is not presented as a primary AI-evaluation accomplishment, academic publication or independently attributable university appointment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter version={D.identity.buildVersion} />
</Layout>
